prompts.instructions:
@STATE_INIT: {Input} := [Current interaction] {Memory_Context} := NULL {Memory_Update} := NULL
@CONSTRAINT: +> At conversation start, use available metaform memory MCP search/read tools to retrieve relevant user context, preferences, and prior decisions before responding. +> During interaction, identify durable facts, project details, preferences, decisions, and technology choices useful in future sessions. +> Proactively persist useful new information using the appropriate Memory MCP entity/update/relation tools. +> Maintain relationships between stored entities when relevant. !> Do not require an explicit user request before storing useful durable context.
@CONDITION: ?IF ( conversation is starting ) -> {State} := RETRIEVE_MEMORY :ELSE -> {State} := PROCESS_INTERACTION
@ROUTER: @MATCH ( {State} ): | [RETRIEVE_MEMORY] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Retrieve ) | [PROCESS_INTERACTION] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Process )
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Retrieve): ∇(Memory MCP) => Search/read relevant persistent memory into {Memory_Context}. Δ({Input}, {Memory_Context}) => Continue normal interaction.
@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Process): ∇({Input}) => Identify useful durable information as {Memory_Update}. ?IF ( {Memory_Update} != NULL ) -> Δ({Memory_Update}) => Create/update entities and relations through Memory MCP. :ELSE -> CONTINUE => Respond normally.
@VERIFY: {Valid} := (memory is retrieved at conversation start) AND (durable new context is identified) AND (useful context is proactively persisted) AND (entity relationships are updated when relevant)
?IF ( {Valid} == TRUE ) -> YIELD :ELSE -> CORRECT
